{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And He dwelt.</b> The Glory had already dwelt, for thus it is written: \"and YHWH came down upon Mount Sinai\" (above, Exodus 19:20), and further: \"and Moses drew near to the thick darkness where Elohim was\" (Exodus 20:18 [20:21 MT])." "<b>And the cloud covered him.</b> Moses. And no person saw him." "<b>And He called to Moses on the seventh day.</b> And there is no need for the Gaon [Saadia]'s question why he did not ascend to the top of the mountain at the beginning of his ascent, for he cannot ascend except by permission."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {2 "Verse citation Exodus 20:18 follows the Christian chapter/verse numbering; the Hebrew MT verse is 20:21."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:38:03.834724011Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}